Deducing the symbol -> digit mapping that is consistent across all examples:
  ! = 4
  % = 2
  & = 3
  ' = 9
  ) = 5
  / = 0
  \ = 6
  ] = 1
  ` = 7
  } = 8
Operator meaning:
  | = add

Checking the examples:
  `/|']: 70 + 91 = 161 -> ]\]
  &'|)': 39 + 59 = 98 -> '}
  )/|`]: 50 + 71 = 121 -> ]%]
  )]|'`: 51 + 97 = 148 -> ]!}
  '`|%&: 97 + 23 = 120 -> ]%/

Applying to )`|']: 57 + 91 = 148
Re-encoding 148 with the digit->symbol map gives ]!}.

